---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service: Try Convi"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Try Convi."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 16 July 2026</p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Try Convi ("the service"), available at{" "}
      <a href="https://tryconvi.com">tryconvi.com</a>. By using the service you
      agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>What Try Convi is</h2>
    <p>
      Try Convi is a language-learning tool with browsable conversation
      scenarios and a Practice mode. It's an educational aid, not a guarantee
      of fluency, and the colloquial phrases and slang it teaches are provided
      for learning and entertainment.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts and access</h2>
    <p>
      Everything is free: every scenario and all of Practice mode, with no
      account and no payment. You can give us an email address if you want to
      hear about the app, and that is the only thing we ever ask for. Your
      access is for your personal, non-commercial use, so please don't scrape,
      resell, or redistribute the content.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Don't misuse the service: no attempting to break, overload, scrape at
      scale, or gain unauthorized access to our systems, and no using the
      content unlawfully.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Try Convi name, content, and design are owned by us. Using the site
      grants you a personal license to use the content, not ownership of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. Language
      is living and regional. We aim for accuracy but can't guarantee every
      phrase fits every situation. Use good judgement, especially with slang.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as the service evolves. Continued use after
      changes means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Email{" "}
      <a href="mailto:hello@tryconvi.com">hello@tryconvi.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal .updated {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
